            "The most important stop rule addresses promising a term, discount, feature, or renewal outcome. When that condition appears, the assistant should preserve the source, note the uncertainty, and route it to the account executive or customer owner. The handoff should say what is known and what is not known. It should never convert a request for preparation into an approval, diagnosis, promise, or conclusion."
